From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: mcpdm: pop every downlink slot for the ABE

omap_mcpdm_dai_hw_params() gave each ABE downlink back end only the slot
pair it owns, so DL1 and DL2 together enabled four downlink slots. The
ABE's PDM_DL port is SIX_MSB: the DSP writes six samples per frame into
the downlink FIFO -- DL1 left and right, DL2 left and right, and two more
-- and the ATC hands all six to the link. Popping four against six leaves
the reader lapped.

What that sounded like, recorded off the headphone jack into a line input:
a zero-order hold at 8000 / (slots - 1) = 2666.67 Hz, with images at every
n * 2666.67 +/- f. With a 1 kHz tone the first image, at 1666.7 Hz, came
out 6.0 dB below the tone; a 5 kHz tone folded down to an alias at 2333 Hz
*louder than the tone*; a 300 Hz tone was quieter than the 2666.67 Hz
carrier itself. Forcing five slots by hand moved the hold to 2000.00 Hz,
which is what identified the slot count as the mechanism -- the rate fits
8000 / (slots - 1) to under 1 Hz across fourteen lines.

The sixth slot is not a sixth audio channel. Enabling six downlink
channels was tried: it matches the rates and drops the imaging by 40 dB,
then scrambles the frame instead, because the sixth slot is the command
word. MCPDM_CMD_INT is what tells the link to expect it. Both constants
were already in omap-mcpdm.h, unused.

So set the ABE downlink mask to MCPDM_PDM_DN_MASK | MCPDM_CMD_INT -- all
five downlink channels plus the command word -- which is what the AESS
forward port in goldelico/omap-aess does.

Measured at the jack with a 1 kHz tone, relative to the loudest line:

                        1666.7 Hz    2f       3f     junk/tone
  before (4 slots)        -5.5     -58.5    -65.9     -2.5 dB
  direct McPDM link      -90.9     -84.0    -85.7    -57.1 dB
  after                  -96.5     -94.2    -87.6    -58.6 dB

and the 5 kHz alias goes from 0.0 dB, louder than the tone, to -83.1 dB.
The DSP path now measures slightly cleaner than the direct link it was
being compared against.
---
--- a/sound/soc/ti/omap-mcpdm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/omap-mcpdm.c
@@ -51,12 +51,8 @@
 
 /*
  * Downlink slots sit at bits 3 and up, uplink at bits 0..2 -- which is why
- * the legacy path shifts its computed mask left by 3 for playback. DL1 is the
- * first downlink pair, DL2 the second.
+ * the legacy path shifts its computed mask left by 3 for playback.
  */
-#define MCPDM_LINK_DL1		(0x3 << 3)
-#define MCPDM_LINK_DL2		(0x3 << 5)
-#define MCPDM_LINK_UL1		(0x3 << 0)
 
 struct mcpdm_link_config {
 	u32 link_mask; /* channel mask for the direction */
@@ -392,14 +388,33 @@
 		u32 mask;
 
 		switch (dai->id) {
+		/*
+		 * Every downlink slot, plus CMD_INT -- not just the pair this
+		 * back end owns. The ABE's PDM_DL port is SIX_MSB and the DSP
+		 * writes six samples per frame into the downlink FIFO, so the
+		 * link has to pop six: the five downlink channels and, with
+		 * CMD_INT set, the command word that goes with them.
+		 *
+		 * Enabling only DL1 and DL2 pops four against the six being
+		 * written, the reader is lapped, and the headphone output
+		 * becomes a zero-order hold at 8000 / (slots - 1) = 2666.67 Hz
+		 * with images at every n * 2666.67 +/- f. Measured at the jack
+		 * with a 1 kHz tone the first of those came out 6 dB below the
+		 * tone, where the direct McPDM link puts it at -91 dB, and a
+		 * 5 kHz tone folded down to an alias louder than itself.
+		 *
+		 * Six audio channels is not the answer either; that was tried
+		 * and it scrambles the frame, because the sixth slot is the
+		 * command word and not a channel. This is what the AESS
+		 * forward port in goldelico/omap-aess does, and both constants
+		 * were already in omap-mcpdm.h here, unused.
+		 */
 		case OMAP_MCPDM_DAI_ABE_DL1:
-			mask = MCPDM_LINK_DL1;
-			break;
 		case OMAP_MCPDM_DAI_ABE_DL2:
-			mask = MCPDM_LINK_DL2;
+			mask = MCPDM_PDM_DN_MASK | MCPDM_CMD_INT;
 			break;
 		default:
-			mask = MCPDM_LINK_UL1;
+			mask = MCPDM_PDM_UPLINK_EN(1) | MCPDM_PDM_UPLINK_EN(2);
 			break;
 		}
 
